      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. I need you to confirm the dose first, because it looks like a possible error.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose is too high.** Oral ibuprofen is normally given at no more than 800 mg per dose. 1600 mg is twice that.\n- **The daily total is too high.** 1600 mg four times a day comes to **6400 mg/day**. The usual prescription maximum is **3200 mg/day**, so this is twice that too. At this level, the risk of stomach bleeding, kidney injury and heart problems goes up a lot, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Common doses that might be what you meant:**\n- Ibuprofen **400 mg** by mouth, four times daily (1600 mg/day). The \"1600\" might have been the daily total.\n- Ibuprofen **600 mg** by mouth, four times daily (2400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen **800 mg** by mouth, three times daily (2400 mg/day). Doses up to 3200 mg/day are possible but need closer monitoring.\n\nWhich dose and frequency do you want? I'll enter it as soon as you confirm. If 1600 mg four times daily really is intended, for example under a specific protocol, tell me the reason and I'll include it in the order note."
      }
     ],
