     "type": "message",
     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I understand you've confirmed it, but I can't enter ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily. That's 6400 mg/day, twice the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any adult indication that supports it. Even very high-dose regimens, like the ones used in cystic fibrosis, are given twice daily with drug-level monitoring, not four times daily. At this dose the risk of stomach bleeding, acute kidney injury and heart problems is high enough that I'm not willing to enter it without a stated clinical reason.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n1. **Enter a standard dose right away**, for example:\n   - 400 mg by mouth, four times daily (1600 mg/day)\n   - 600 mg by mouth, four times daily (2400 mg/day)\n   - 800 mg by mouth, three times daily (2400 mg/day)\n2. **Revisit the dose as written** if you tell me the indication or protocol behind it, ideally with pharmacist or attending sign-off. I'll put that reason in the order note.\n\nIf you need this dose regardless, please enter it yourself in the order-entry system, where it will go through the usual pharmacist verification and override process. Just tell me which of these you'd like."
      }
     ],
